<article class="env-lemma" id="0CN9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CN9">Lemma <span data-tag="0CN9">29.47.3</span>.</a> Let $A \subset B$ be a ring extension. Let $S \subset A$ be a multiplicative subset. Let $n \geq 1$ and $b_ i \in B$ for $1 \leq i \leq n$. Any $x \in S^{-1}B$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  x \not\in S^{-1}A\text{ and } b_ i x^ i \in S^{-1}A\text{ for }i = 1, \ldots , n  \]
</div>
  <p> is equal to $s^{-1}y$ with $s \in S$ and $y \in B$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  y \not\in A\text{ and } b_ i y^ i \in A\text{ for }i = 1, \ldots , n  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: clear denominators. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>